<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander III of Imereti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1660">1660</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander III was King of Imereti in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> from 1639 to 1660. Much of his reign was spent in conflict with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levan-ii-dadiani">Levan II Dadiani</a>, the powerful prince of Mingrelia, and he sought the protection of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> against his rivals and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>. After Levan's death in 1657 he briefly extended his authority over Mingrelia, but his gains did not outlast his own death in 1660.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-iii-of-imereti.jpg" alt="Alexander III of Imereti" width="320" height="499" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Teramo Castelli · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexander_III_by_Castelli.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
